## DESCRIPTION
## Calculate the product of matrices if they exist.
## ENDDESCRIPTION


## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Matrices)
## DBsection(Matrix algebra)
## Date(September 5, 2008)
## Institution(Fitchburg State University)
## Author(Peter Staab)
## KEYWORDS('matrices', 'matrix product')

# updated 2024.01.05

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',             'PGML.pl',
    'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context("Numeric");

$A = Matrix([ map { [ map { random(-6, 6) } (1 .. 2) ] } (1 .. 3) ]);
$B = Matrix([ map { [ map { random(-6, 6) } (1 .. 2) ] } (1 .. 2) ]);
$C = Matrix([ map { [ map { random(-6, 6) } (1 .. 3) ] } (1 .. 2) ]);

$rma1 = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ['The product \(AB\) does not exist'],
        [ 'The product \(AB\) is the 3 by 2 matrix %s*', $A * $B ],
        [
            'The product \(AB\) is the 2 by 3 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0, 0 ] ])
        ]
    ],
    1
);

$rma2 = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ['The product \(AC\) does not exist'],
        [
            'The product \(AC\) is the 3 by 2 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0 ] ])
        ],
        [
            'The product \(AC\) is the 2 by 3 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0, 0 ] ])
        ],
        [
            'The product \(AC\) is the 2 by 2 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0 ] ])
        ],
        [ 'The product \(AC\) is the 3 by 3 matrix %s*', $A * $C ],
    ],
    4
);

$rma3 = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ['The product \(CA\) does not exist'],
        [
            'The product \(CA\) is the 3 by 2 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0 ] ])
        ],
        [
            'The product \(CA\) is the 2 by 3 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0, 0 ] ])
        ],

        [ 'The product \(CA\) is the 2 by 2 matrix %s*', $C * $A ],
        [
            'The product \(CA\) is the 3 by 3 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0, 0 ] ])
        ],

    ],
    3

);

$rma4 = RadioMultiAnswer(
    [
        ['The product \(CB\) does not exist'],
        [
            'The product \(CB\) is the 3 by 2 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0 ] ])
        ],
        [
            'The product \(CB\) is the 2 by 3 matrix %s*',
            Matrix([ [ 0, 0, 0 ], [ 0, 0, 0 ] ])
        ]
    ],
    0
);

BEGIN_PGML

Let 

[``` 
\begin{aligned}
A & = [$A] & B & = [$B] & C & = [$C]
\end{aligned}
```]

Find the following matrix products if they exist.  For each product you will need to determine the size of the result as well. 

1) [_]{$rma1}
2) [_]{$rma2}
3) [_]{$rma3}
4) [_]{$rma4}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Recall that for the product of two matrices, the number of columns of the first must equal
the number of columns of the second.  Another way to put this if [`A`] is a [`m \times p`] matrix and [`B`] is a [`p \times n`] matrix, then the product is valid (the inner 
dimensions are the same) and the result is a [`m \times n`] matrix.  

To calculate the [`i`]th row and [`j`]th column of [`AB`], then find the dot product
between the [`i`]th row of [`A`] and the [`j`]th column of [`B`]. 

1) The product of a [`3 \times 2`] matrix and a [`2 \times 2`] matrix 
is a [`3 \times 2`] matrix and the product is 
[``` AB = [$A*$B]```]
2) The product of a [`3 \times 2`] matrix and a [`2 \times 3`] matrix 
is a [`3 \times 3`] matrix and the product is 
[``` AC = [$A*$C]```]
3) The product of a [`2 \times 3`] matrix and a [`3 \times 2`] matrix 
is a [`2 \times 2`] matrix and the product is 
[``` CA = [$C*$A]```]
4) The product between a [` 2 \times 3`] matrix and a [` 2 \times 2 `] matrix does not exist.

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
